        "title": "Watchmaking - 00 Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Horology — the science and art of measuring time — is one of the oldest and most technically demanding fields in human history. The central challenge has never changed: **any physical oscillator degrades**. Temperature, wear, gravity, friction, magnetic fields, and atmospheric pressure all perturb the frequency of whatever mechanism you're using to divide time into equal intervals."
    },
